and EOSIO/eos code originally distributed under the MIT License.

Additional embedded and vendored third-party notices are listed in
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES. File-level source lineage and compatibility-only donor
boundaries are documented in PROVENANCE.md.

`vendor/libsodium/upstream` is an unmodified extraction of the official
libsodium 1.0.22 release archive. Forge compiles only its portable XSalsa20
subset as a private backend for `forge_crypto_symmetric`; the exact archive and
source-file hashes are recorded in `vendor/libsodium/MANIFEST.md`.

`libraries/vm/wasm/interpret` is a derived native port of AntelopeIO/eos-vm and is
distributed under EOS VM License V1.0. The complete license is preserved in
`libraries/vm/wasm/interpret/LICENSE.eos-vm`.

The experimental replacement vendors WebAssembly Micro Runtime (WAMR) from
the SystasisIO/wasm-micro-runtime fork. Its upstream license is Apache License
2.0 with LLVM Exceptions, preserved in `vendor/wamr/LICENSE`. Fork provenance
and the pinned revision are recorded in `docs/donors/forge-wamr-fork-v1.md`.

`guest/libraries/runtime/details/allocator.hxx` is derived from AntelopeIO/cdt and
EOSIO/eosio.cdt under the MIT License. Forge Contract SDK release archives also
redistribute an unmodified LLVM/Clang/lld/libc++/compiler-rt toolchain under the
upstream Apache License 2.0 with LLVM Exceptions. Exact pins and boundaries are
recorded in `PROVENANCE.md` and `THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES`.

